        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The paper is organized as follows. Section 2 introduces affine integral excitation and its scalar form. Section 3 formulates the problem setting for a polynomial vector field on a compact invariant set. Section 4 presents the main result on the absence of sticking to hyperplanes and affine IPE. Sections 5 and 5.1 consider a resonant triad model and the application of the main theorem to it. Section 6 Concludes the article and is devoted to the development of work ideas. The proof of the main theorem is deferred to the appendix.",
            "block_bbox": [
